  "document": {
    "title": "Device/media I/O moved to iiDeviceMultimedia",
    "role": "guide",
    "authority": "markdown_source"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b000001",
      "kind": "heading",
      "start_line": 1,
      "end_line": 1,
      "raw": "# Device/media I/O moved to iiDeviceMultimedia\n",
      "level": 1,
      "title": "Device/media I/O moved to iiDeviceMultimedia"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000002",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 2,
      "end_line": 2,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 3,
      "end_line": 5,
      "raw": "Since iiSDKCore 0.12.0, USB/HID, BLE central/GATT, float32 PCM, MIDI UMP,\ntheir protocol parsers and native platform backends are owned by the independent\n[iiDeviceMultimedia](../../iiDeviceMultimedia/README.md) package.\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000004",
      "kind": "blank",
      "start_line": 6,
      "end_line": 6,
      "raw": "\n"
    },
    {
      "id": "b000005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "start_line": 7,
      "end_line": 11,
      "raw": "The complete [hardware contract](../../iiDeviceMultimedia/docs/hardware.md) and\n[migration guide](device-extraction.md) describe current APIs and support limits.\nCore retains EventLoop, FrameLoop, Runtime, TaskScope, Thread, Channel and AsyncIO\nand has no dependency on the new module. Device 0.2 is likewise independent of\nCore; the application owns the connection through ii::device::Hardware::poll().\n"
    }
  ],
